+# USDC Pay
+
+A single-page dApp for sending [USDC](https://etherscan.io/token/0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48)
+on Ethereum mainnet. Connect a wallet, enter a recipient and an amount, send.
+The page shows your USDC balance and your ETH balance, since gas is paid in ETH.
+
+## Stack
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Framework | Next.js 16 (App Router, Turbopack, React 19) |
+| Chain access | wagmi 2 + viem 2 |
+| Wallets | RainbowKit 2 |
+| Data | TanStack Query 5 |
+| Styling | Tailwind CSS 4 |
+| Language | TypeScript (strict) |
+
+RainbowKit 2.2 peer-depends on `wagmi@^2.9`, so this pins wagmi 2.19 rather than
+wagmi 3. That is the combination with the most production mileage today; moving
+to wagmi 3 means waiting for a RainbowKit release or swapping the wallet UI.
+
+## Running it
+
+```bash
+npm install
+cp .env.example .env.local   # then fill it in
+npm run dev                  # http://localhost:3000/pay
+```
+
+| Script | |
+| --- | --- |
+| `npm run dev` | dev server |
+| `npm run build` | production build (also type-checks) |
+| `npm run start` | serve the production build |
+| `npm test` | unit tests for the money-handling logic |
+| `npm run lint` | ESLint |
+| `npm run typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |
+
+### Environment
+
+Both variables are optional to *build*, but you want both in production:
+
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID` — from [Reown Cloud](https://cloud.reown.com).
+  Without it only browser-extension wallets can connect; the UI says so rather
+  than failing when someone taps a mobile wallet.
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC_URL` — Alchemy/Infura/your own node. Without it the
+  app falls back to viem's public endpoint, which is heavily rate-limited and
+  will make balances and gas estimates flaky under any real traffic.
+
+## How USDC is treated
+
+USDC is not a generic ERC-20, and the details it gets wrong most often are the
+ones this app is careful about:
+
+- **6 decimals, not 18.** `decimals()` is read from the contract rather than
+  hardcoded (USDC sits behind an upgradeable proxy), and the form will not parse
+  an amount until that read lands. Amounts are parsed from strings straight to
+  `bigint` — no floats anywhere in the path from keystroke to calldata.
+- **Transfers revert rather than returning `false`.** USDC can be paused, and
+  either party can be blacklisted. Every transfer is simulated with
+  `useSimulateContract` before the wallet is opened, so those failures show up
+  as a sentence in the form instead of a burnt gas fee.
+- **Balances are read on mainnet regardless of the wallet's current network**,
+  so a user on the wrong chain still sees their real position — plus a prompt to
+  switch before they can send.
+
+## Product decisions worth knowing
+
+- **Recipients** accept an address or an ENS name. Mixed-case addresses have
+  their EIP-55 checksum verified, which catches a single mistyped character;
+  all-lowercase input has no checksum to check, so it is accepted and
+  normalised. Pasted addresses get a reverse-ENS lookup as confirmation.
+- **The zero address and the USDC contract itself are hard-blocked.** Sending to
+  either destroys the money.
+- **A contract recipient is a warning, not a block** — it may be a smart account
+  (fine) or a contract that cannot move USDC back out (not fine). The user
+  decides.
+- **Gas is surfaced, not assumed.** The estimated network fee is shown before
+  signing, having no ETH blocks the send outright, and having *probably* too
+  little warns.
+- **Errors are quiet until they are real.** Half-typed addresses and `0.` do not
+  flash red; they just leave the button disabled.
+- **Wallet errors are translated.** A user rejection reads as "You rejected the
+  request in your wallet", not a 40-line viem stack.
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+src/
+  app/
+    layout.tsx           root shell; forwards the cookie header for SSR rehydration
+    page.tsx             redirects / → /pay
+    pay/page.tsx         the page
+    providers.tsx        wagmi + TanStack Query + RainbowKit
+  components/
+    pay-form.tsx         the form, its states and the send flow
+    balances.tsx         USDC + ETH balance panel
+    tx-status.tsx        signing / confirming / sent / reverted
+    header.tsx, ui.tsx
+  hooks/
+    use-balances.ts      USDC balance, ETH balance, token decimals
+    use-recipient.ts     address + ENS resolution and recipient checks
+    use-transfer-gas.ts  gas limit and fee estimate for this transfer
+  lib/
+    usdc.ts              token address, ABI, chain
+    amount.ts            string → base units (unit-tested)
+    address.ts           address parsing and recipient rules (unit-tested)
+    format.ts            display formatting (unit-tested)
+    errors.ts            viem errors → human sentences
+    wagmi.ts             chains, transports, connectors
+```
+
+`src/stubs/x402.cjs` aliases four optional peer dependencies that RainbowKit's
+barrel reaches through the Base Account connector and this app never executes.
+Without the alias the bundler fails to resolve them; see `next.config.ts`.
+
+## Tests
+
+`npm test` (Node's built-in runner) covers the pure logic where a mistake costs
+someone money: decimal scaling, precision limits, checksum validation, blocked
+recipients, and the display formatter's rule that balances truncate rather than
+round up.
+
+Wallet-level flows are not covered — they need a forked-mainnet E2E harness
+(Anvil + Playwright), which is the obvious next piece of work.
+
+## Known gaps
+
+- Mainnet only. Adding L2s means a chain selector and a per-chain USDC address
+  map, not just another entry in `chains`.
+- No transaction history; the app shows the current send, not past ones.
+- No fiat conversion — amounts are USDC, not "dollars".
+- `useWaitForTransactionReceipt` waits for one confirmation and does not handle
+  a wallet-side speed-up/cancel replacing the hash.
